@@ -61,12 +61,13 @@ signal_op_off_its_node	GUARD	-	compiler invariant: a Signal op matches its SIGNA
 sim_blocked_command	LIMIT	-	docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-phase-6-1-loose-ends.md section 4 (a wait only a command's peer can end is refused in sim): a command runs on the baton under a real-time bound, block= (2 s by default), and any command slower than it is refused, whether it waits on another activity or is only slow; timing-dependent by nature, and block= is how a program with slow commands runs under sim
 sim_blocked_native	LIMIT	-	docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-phase-6-1-loose-ends.md section 4 (a wait only a native's own thread or a peer can end is refused in sim): a native call that leaves its driver runs on the baton under block=, past which the interpreter's thread is signalled once and the call refused once it returns; any such call slower than the bound is refused, timing-dependent by nature; a native that retries on EINTR or blocks outside a system call stays unbounded, and so does a native call under a pin, which does not leave its driver (it hangs on the oracle too)
 sim_endless_wait	LIMIT	-	docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-phase-6-1-loose-ends.md section 4: a deadlock in the simulation mode is a loud refusal; virtual time cannot end a wait only a real signal can
